---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Quickstart from '../../figures/06-quickstart.astro';

const DOCS = 'https://gitlab.com/dunn.dev/tower/-/blob/main/docs/';

// docs/setup.md is written for the forge: its h1 is this page's title, and its relative links resolve against docs/ there.
const setup = await getEntry('docs', 'setup');
if (!setup?.rendered) throw new Error('docs/setup.md did not render');
const html = setup.rendered.html
  .replace(/<h1[^>]*>.*?<\/h1>/s, '')
  .replace(/href="(?![a-z]+:|#|\/)([^"]*)"/gi, (_, url) => `href="${new URL(url, DOCS).href}"`);
---
<Layout title="Install" description="Deploy tower, add checks, and set up alerts, heartbeats, relays and upgrades.">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">Install</h1>
  </header>
  <div class="cat-explainer figure-pair">
    <Quickstart />
  </div>
  <article class="doc">
    <p>One command deploys an instance directory. It validates the config, applies the D1 migrations, deploys the prober, then builds and deploys the page. The hostname needs a proxied DNS record in its zone. The first round of checks follows, and tower mails DEPLOYED. The sections below give the commands, then alerts, heartbeats, relays, self-checks and upgrades.</p>
    <Fragment set:html={html} />
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .doc { max-width: 46rem; color: var(--text-2); line-height: 1.7; }
  .doc :global(h2) { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-2xl); color: var(--text); margin: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-4); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .doc :global(h3) { font-size: var(--text-lg); color: var(--text); margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-3); }
  .doc :global(p), .doc :global(ul), .doc :global(ol), .doc :global(pre), .doc :global(table) { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .doc :global(ul), .doc :global(ol) { padding-left: var(--space-5); }
  .doc :global(li) { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .doc :global(li > p) { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .doc :global(pre) { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: var(--space-4); color: var(--text); }
  .doc :global(:not(pre) > code) { background: var(--surface); padding: 0.1em 0.4em; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
</style>
